                <pb facs="0243" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg147"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">A decree published in the manuscript Pekin Gazette,
                        June 10, 1900.</hi></head>
                <p>Let Prince Tuan (Tsai I) be appointed president of the Tsungli Yamen. Let Chi
                    Hsiu, president of the board of rites, Pu Hsing, junior vice-president of the
                    board of works, and Na Tung, subchancellor of the grand secretariat and holding
                    the brevet rank of vice-president of the board of rites, be appointed ministers
                    to the Tsungli Yamen.</p>
                <p>At the present time we are confronted with difficulties and troublesome
                    questions, and it is absolutely necessary that the said prince and ministers
                    should sincerely apply their minds to the performance of the duties of their
                    post so as to aid us. They will not be permitted to decline appointment.</p>
            </div>
